From 48af1034008a31666afc1646dc2bdb6e40f174e6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 19:20:24 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix(sim): draw lathe chuck bores inscribed so the collision
 solid never drops steel

The chuck bore polygon had its flats on the bore circle, leaving its
vertices up to 0.12 % of the bore radius outside the true bore: steel
missing from the collision solid. Bores now have their vertices on the
circle (inscribed); outer faces keep their flats on it (circumscribed).
The module comment said the opposite of what the code did; corrected.

The sim envelope test now probes 1e-3 mm inside every true face and
outside every true bore wall at every vertex and flat middle, and air
1e-3 mm past each face's tessellation allowance, instead of 0.5-1 mm
off the rim and jaw tip.

Fixes #1470

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
